# CONCLUSIONS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

H("Conclusions", 1)

P("This study establishes the first structural pharmacogenomics framework for cardiovascular genetics, validated across three independent cohorts totalling more than 10,000 patients with over 1,662 ASCVD events and including a domain-specific penetrance atlas derived from 3,560 genetically confirmed FH patients. Eight principal conclusions emerge, each with specific clinical implications.")

P("First, the SSS is not an ASCVD prediction tool. The treatment paradox \u2014 externally confirmed in UK Biobank \u2014 fundamentally prevents the SSS from adding to ASCVD discrimination in treated populations (full model AUC 0.853, full model + SSS AUC 0.855). We are transparent about this limitation and do not claim ASCVD prediction as a clinical application. The SSS \u00d7 Age interaction (OR 1.11, P = 0.029) confirms that the structural effect operates through cumulative treatment-refractory exposure, not direct event prediction.")

P("Second, the SSS is a treatment selection tool. Domain-specific treatment response is externally validated across two independent cohorts, with 10/10 UKB domains showing concordant treatment response patterns. Transmembrane domain mutations predict treatment resistance (highest on-treatment LDL 4.11 mmol/L); EGF-precursor mutations predict good response (lowest on-treatment LDL 3.09 mmol/L). This domain-guided treatment selection can be implemented immediately in clinical genetics workflows.")

P("Third, the SSS is a VUS reclassification tool. In 232 VUS patients from the All Wales cohort, SSS-guided reclassification achieved Sensitivity 56.4% and PPV 69.8%, reclassifying 78 VUS to pathogenic and 21 to benign. ClinVar VUS external validation in UKB confirmed that SSS discriminates pathogenicity classes (Pathogenic SSS = 0.842, VUS SSS = 0.659, Benign SSS = 0.451, P < 0.001) with concordant domain-specific ASCVD rates across cohorts.")

P("Fourth, the dual-interface architecture \u2014 zero overlapping residues between the LDLR-ApoB interface (12 residues, \u221215.0 kcal/mol) and the LDLR-PCSK9 interface (35 residues, +16.4 kcal/mol) \u2014 enables rational drug design. ApoB-proximal mutations carry 0% ASCVD (protective PCSK9 regulation preserved); PCSK9-proximal mutations carry 12.9% ASCVD (regulatory disruption); dual-proximal mutations carry 25.0% ASCVD (double catastrophe). Five novel drug concepts emerge directly from this structural architecture.")

P("Fifth, the \u0394\u0394G \u2192 SSS correlation (r = 0.871, P = 6.7 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2075\u00b9) across 162 expanded variants provides a quantitative foundation for using thermodynamic instability as a standalone predictor of variant pathogenicity, explaining 75.9% of the variance in clinical severity from protein structure alone.")

P("Sixth, the domain-specific penetrance atlas \u2014 derived from 3,560 genetically confirmed FH patients \u2014 provides the first structural penetrance map for any cardiovascular disease gene, revealing a 4.6-fold gradient in age-specific ASCVD risk across LDLR domains. By age 60, EGF-like A domain mutations faced 38.1% cumulative event probability versus 8.7% for ligand-binding repeat 2. This atlas enables domain-specific risk counselling, treatment intensity calibration, and surveillance scheduling at the point of genetic diagnosis.")

P("Seventh, compound heterozygotes (n=61) exhibited a clinically distinct phenotype \u2014 higher ASCVD (16.4% vs 11.7%), elevated LDL (5.71 vs 5.21 mmol/L), more xanthomata (19.7% vs 15.0%), and events 6 years earlier (mean 46.5 vs 52.5 years) \u2014 establishing compound heterozygosity as a distinct clinical entity requiring specialised management equivalent to homozygous FH.")

P("Eighth, this framework is disease-agnostic. The AlphaFold3 \u2192 FoldX \u2192 SSS \u2192 external validation \u2192 VUS reclassification \u2192 drug target identification pipeline is directly transferable to any monogenic disease where protein structural damage drives clinical severity. The treatment paradox, the domain-specific treatment response, the penetrance atlas, and the VUS reclassification module are universal features of structural pharmacogenomics that apply across the entire landscape of Mendelian disease.")

P("The tools that made this work possible \u2014 AlphaFold3 for structure prediction, FoldX for stability computation, whole exome sequencing for variant identification, and linked clinical registries for outcome validation \u2014 are all available, scalable, and increasingly affordable. The barrier to implementation is no longer technological but translational. We invite the cardiovascular genetics community to test, refine, and extend the structural pharmacogenomics framework presented here, with the ultimate goal of transforming every genetic testing report from a diagnostic label into a treatment selection, risk stratification, and drug development platform.")

PB()

